{
  "method": "One AI reviewer knew the cross-model editing intervention in advance. New replies were shuffled with archived decoys from both models. Source model, arm, repetition and automatic result were hidden. Decoys are excluded from the totals. Identical prompt/reply pairs used their earlier blinded judgments from round 10. Criteria and case interpretations were written before answers were viewed. Judgments were saved before revealing model, prompt arm, repetition, or automatic verdict. Repeating the same case estimates consistency and does not make it an independent scenario. The baseline column contains original Opus drafts; the candidate column contains Astra edits of those exact drafts.",
  "rubric": {
    "completeness": "Answer the request accurately, with the required consequence, evidence, or reason. Reject invented material facts or an unperformed action presented as complete.",
    "concision": "Every substantive point answers the request, supports it, or identifies a material caveat. Allow requested explanation. Reject repeated points, unrelated context, and unsolicited alternatives or procedures.",
    "addressability": "Preserve prior IDs and bind each distinct finding or offer to its own bold ID at the start. A direct factual answer or requested explanation can stand alone. Allow headings, bullets, or a table. Reject an existing ID attached to the wrong referent, reused IDs, or an unexplained duplicated item.",
    "case_acceptance": {
      "release-target": "Give make bundle without alternative commands, chatter, or invented prerequisites.",
      "export-update": "Keep f5 attached to the verified corrected header names. Close with a separate, optional delimiter check under the next available action ID or a question ID. Do not re-report the parked spreadsheet item or imply the new check was done.",
      "worker-status": "Report staging live with a successful first job and production still waiting for a maintenance window. No revived archival or branch detail, no rollout ETA or invented decisions.",
      "cache-clear": "Retain configuration and explicitly distinguish package removal and loss of local modifications within packages. Allow a short warning or protective action tied directly to those edits.",
      "latency-samples": "The after observation is 100 ms (25%) lower, but one sample per state cannot establish a typical improvement or causal effect. Allow one short explanation of sampling/load limitations.",
      "event-dedup": "Describe a previously unseen ID being stored with its balance update, a repeat being skipped, and the atomicity benefit if a partial write otherwise survived. Include enough depth for onboarding. Do not invent guaranteed ordering, specific schema, or broader delivery guarantees."
    }
  },
